  "name": "Mind Flay",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/svg/daze.svg",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You wreathe the mind of a creature you can see within range. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 2d6 psychic damage or half as much on a successful one.</p><p>In addition to the damage, a creature who failed the saving throw has disadvantage on all attack rolls and ability checks for the spells duration. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can reroll the Wisdom saving throw, ending this effect on a success.</p><p><strong><em>At Higher Levels.</em></strong> When you cast this spell using a spell slot of 3rd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d6 for each slot level above 2nd.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
